The noop coroutine frame's resume and destroy slots take the frame.

libstdc++ has no __builtin_coro_noop, so std::noop_coroutine() is a plain C++
object: a static __frame whose first two words are function pointers that the
generated code calls the way it calls any coroutine's.  The generated call is
`frame->__r (frame)' -- resume takes the frame pointer, which is how a
coroutine finds its own state -- but the header declares the slots as
`void (*) ()' and fills them with a `__dummy_resume_destroy ()' that takes
nothing.  On every target with a C calling convention that is harmless: the
extra argument is passed and ignored.

wasm type-checks call_indirect against the function's declared signature at
run time, so there it is not harmless.  The callee's .functype is `() -> ()',
the call site's type is `(i32) -> ()', and the resume traps with
`null function or function signature mismatch' -- which names the slot as
empty when it is in fact occupied by a function of the wrong type.

Fixed in the header rather than by giving GCC a __builtin_coro_noop, because
the slots' type is simply wrong about what writes to and reads from them and
is not a property of any target: the pointer width is unchanged, so the
frame's layout is identical on every target and no ABI moves.  Nothing else
in libstdc++ names __r, __d or __dummy_resume_destroy; they exist only to be
read by generated code, which is the code this disagreed with.

Measured: the engine's first scenario run trapped at scenario.wasm 0x7abafb,
`call_indirect 2' in wrap_run_task<...>.actor, which is the symmetric transfer
out of AsyncTask.cppm:235's `return std::noop_coroutine ()' -- the arm
final_awaiter takes when a task started by task::start has no continuation.
The assembly either side of the trap is `call coroutine_handle<>::address',
`i32.load 0', `call_indirect (i32) -> ()', against
`.functype ...__dummy_resume_destroy () -> ()' in the same unit.

Upstream: worth offering, since the declaration is wrong everywhere and only
this target can tell.

--- a/libstdc++-v3/include/std/coroutine
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/include/std/coroutine
@@ -301,10 +301,10 @@
 
       struct __frame
       {
-	static void __dummy_resume_destroy() { }
+	static void __dummy_resume_destroy(void*) { }
 
-	void (*__r)() = __dummy_resume_destroy;
-	void (*__d)() = __dummy_resume_destroy;
+	void (*__r)(void*) = __dummy_resume_destroy;
+	void (*__d)(void*) = __dummy_resume_destroy;
 	struct noop_coroutine_promise __p;
       };
